Perfect! I found the issue now. Look at the `findActiveByMonitorId` method:

```typescript
findActiveByMonitorId = async (monitorId: string, teamId: string): Promise<Incident | null> => {
	const incident = await IncidentModel.findOne({
		monitorId: new mongoose.Types.ObjectId(monitorId),
		teamId: new mongoose.Types.ObjectId(teamId),
		status: true,  // <-- LOOKING FOR status: true (which means RESOLVED/CLOSED!)
	});
	if (!incident) {
		return null;
	}
	return this.toEntity(incident);
};
```

The `findActiveByMonitorId` method is looking for `status: true` which means RESOLVED/CLOSED incidents, not ACTIVE ones!

This is the bug! An "active" incident should have `status: false`, not `status: true`. We need to fix this method to look for `status: false`.

Let me fix this.

